<h1 class="article-title">First Auction Announced for the Sale of an Industrial Building in Liepāja Industrial Park</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>As development of the Liepāja Industrial Park continues on the site of the former Liepājas metalurgs plant, the Liepāja Special Economic Zone (Liepāja SEZ) Authority has announced its first property auction. This is the next step in involving businesses in renewing and transforming the industrial area, offering the opportunity to purchase production buildings. The auction will run from 29 July to 28 August 2025.</p><p>“We initially consolidated all properties on the former Liepājas metalurgs site, developed a local spatial plan and began constructing streets and utility networks. The area is gradually being reintegrated into the city, making it accessible to the public and attractive to investors. It already contains various industrial buildings, for which we will seek new owners through auctions, owners who will renovate and rebuild them to suit a modern green-economy business environment,” says Liepāja SEZ Manager Uldis Hmieļevskis.</p><p> </p><p>Auction property:</p><ul><li>Address: 98A Brīvības Street, Liepāja</li><li>Land: total area 5,132 m²</li><li>Existing building: steam workshop, total area 2,239 m²</li><li>Starting price: EUR 142,000</li><li>Bid increment: EUR 1,420</li></ul><p> </p><p>As Liepāja Mayor Gunārs Ansiņš said when construction began at the Liepāja Industrial Park: “By demolishing the old gatehouse, which once controlled entry to the Liepājas metalurgs site, we are symbolically turning a new page in Liepāja’s industrial history. I hope that, in the years to come, this area will become one of the strongest green industrial parks in Latvia.”</p><p>The Liepāja Industrial Park is being developed on the site of the former Liepājas metalurgs plant, for which a local spatial plan has been prepared. The development covers approximately 120 hectares and includes the construction of eight new streets, which are planned to be opened to public access.</p><p>Phase 1 of the project “Development of Liepāja Industrial Park Infrastructure” is being implemented using EUR 10 million in funding from the Recovery and Resilience Facility, in accordance with the prepared design. Following the procurement results, A-Land will carry out two construction projects and CTB Ltd one. The project involves constructing three sections of streets with utilities (water supply, domestic wastewater drainage, stormwater drainage and district heating networks). At the same time, AS Sadales tīkls is installing the electricity distribution networks.</p><p>The Liepāja Industrial Park is being developed by the Liepāja SEZ Authority and Liepāja City Municipality on the former Liepājas metalurgs site between Brīvības, Meldru, Ezermalas, Parka and Zemnieku streets in Liepāja. It borders Lake Liepāja, a specially protected Natura 2000 site. Under the approved development strategy, the aim is to attract more than EUR 275 million in private investment and create at least 1,500 new jobs.</p><p> </p><p>Auction notice: https://liepaja-sez.lv/lv/iepirkumi-un-izsoles/liepajas-sez-parvalde-riko-elektronisko-izsoli-ar-augsupejosu-soli-nekustamam-ipasumam-bri</p></div>
